fix: mobile nav, hero spacing, and the doodle layer's reach

Four small-screen faults, one of them the cause of two others.

The mobile menu panel was rendering as an 80px strip with its content
pushed above the fold, so only the first link was on screen and nothing
below it could be reached. The panel is `fixed inset-0`, but it renders
inside the nav bar, and the bar carries a translate for its
hide-on-scroll — a transformed ancestor becomes the containing block for
a fixed descendant, so `inset-0` resolved against the 80px bar rather
than the viewport. The panel is now portaled to <body>, which puts it
back on the viewport and makes it a full 844px.

That also explains why there was no way out of the menu: the close
control existed but sat off-screen with everything else. The panel now
carries its own dismiss in the top right, and sits at z-60 above the
nav's z-50 so the bar cannot paint over it.

The trigger becomes a hamburger rather than the word "Menu" — three
rules that morph into a cross while the panel is open, so one control
reads as both affordances.

The hero's mobile top padding drops from 18svh to 7rem: at 18svh the
headline was pushed most of a screen down behind an apparently empty
band. The section also goes full height on a phone, because the doodle
layer fills the section and at 82svh it stopped short of the fold and
left a bare white strip above the photographs. With the section now
full height the type centres rather than sitting at the bottom, where
it fell past the fold.

The menu carries the texture too, so opening it does not drop the reader
onto a plain white sheet.

Verified at 390px on the home, gallery and podcast pages: the panel
opens to full height, every link is reachable, the close control
dismisses it, no page overflows, and no errors or failed requests. The
hamburger stays hidden at 1440.
